V13 (quick-edit route) is complete, and the merge gate now passes.

## Merge gate (the failure that was fixed)
`.jgatefail.txt` reported: MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity.
Ran `git merge manus-parity`; two files conflicted and were resolved keeping BOTH sides:
- `src/index.ts`: kept the V13 quick-edit route (`planQuickEditRoute(effectiveCfg, effectivePrompt)` and
  `quickEditRoute.suffix` / `quickEditRoute.model` wiring) AND the incoming manus-parity memory
  index summary (`memoryIndexSummary` from `memory.indexSummary(8)`, kept in the prompt suffix array).
- `src/tools/multiEdit.ts`: kept the V13 exports/doc comments on `DiffHunk` and `diffLines` (the
  incoming side only had a shorter comment; no code was lost).
Resolution committed as `7d52e7c merge manus-parity: keep quick-edit route with memory index summary (V13)`.
`git merge-tree --write-tree manus-parity HEAD` is clean (exit 0), so no conflict re-emerges.

## What V13 delivers (commit 639a92c)
- `src/agent/quickEdit.ts`: conservative classifier. Measured scope wins (text-only or pure reorder,
  within limits) -> fast model; behavioural / structural / file-boundary / oversized / multi-file /
  ambiguous -> base model. Short instructions classified by narrow-vs-big patterns in English and
  Arabic; ambiguous or long instructions stay on the base model.
- `resolveQuickEditModel` uses the configured fast tier (`fallbackModel`), falling back to the base
  model when it is unset; `planQuickEditRoute` adds a minimal targeted-edit instruction (English +
  Arabic) only for the quick route.
- `planTargetedDiff(before, after)` turns a before/after pair into line-anchored patches (replacement,
  deletion, insertion, insert-before-first-line) via the now-exported `diffLines`/`DiffSummary`/`DiffHunk`.
- Arabic/RTL: narrow-edit instructions are recognised in Arabic, `hasRtlScript` detects RTL script,
  and a targeted patch preserves Arabic text exactly (covered by tests).
- `src/agent/loop.ts` and `src/agent/orchestrator.ts`: optional per-run `model` override so the
  quick-edit route can actually run on the fast model; `src/index.ts` passes it through.

## Gates (all run from the worktree root)
- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> clean
- `npm run build:server` -> dist/server.cjs built, pdf worker copied
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)` -> compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages generated
- `node --import tsx --test src/agent/__tests__/*.test.ts` -> 144 pass, 0 fail
- `node --import tsx --test src/tools/__tests__/*.test.ts` -> 435 pass, 0 fail
  (includes quickEdit, editSchemaAlias, findAndEdit, fileLock, mapReduce)

Working tree is clean; no existing test was weakened.
